# {{JOB_NAME}} — Alibaba Cloud Flink Deployment Artifacts

For a new project, place this file in the project root. For an existing project, integrate these sections into its established deployment documentation. Replace every `{{...}}` value and remove unused conditional files or rows before delivery. Do not place secret values in the project artifacts.

## Directory Structure

```text
{{PROJECT_ROOT}}/
├── README.md
├── src/
│   └── {{JOB_CODE}}
├── scripts/
│   ├── package_code.sh          # Packages modular job code into the job ZIP
│   └── build_dependencies.sh    # Builds third-party packages into deps.zip
├── requirements.txt             # Include only for third-party Python packages
└── artifacts/
    ├── {{JOB_ARCHIVE}}          # Include for modular code after packaging
    └── deps.zip                 # Include only after a successful dependency build
```

`scripts/package_code.sh` is required only for modular jobs. It packages deployable project code while preserving Python import paths at the ZIP root; it excludes third-party dependencies, environments, caches, tests not used at runtime, and generated artifacts.

`scripts/build_dependencies.sh` is required only when the job uses Python packages that are not pre-installed in VVR. It uses the `quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_28_x86_64` Docker image to install the pinned packages for the confirmed Python version, then packages the contents of `__pypackages__` as `artifacts/deps.zip`.

Describe any runtime files or JARs that are delivered outside this core tree.

