## Build the Upload Artifacts

### Modular code only

Run `bash scripts/package_code.sh src artifacts/{{JOB_ARCHIVE}} {{ENTRY_MODULE}}`, then inspect the archive with `python3 -m zipfile -l artifacts/{{JOB_ARCHIVE}}`.

The archive root must contain the import path for `{{ENTRY_MODULE}}`. Upload this archive as **Python File Path (Python 文件地址)**.

### Third-party Python packages only

Confirm an x86-64 target, a glibc baseline compatible with manylinux 2.28, and the Python version before running:

Run `bash scripts/build_dependencies.sh {{PYTHON_VERSION}} requirements.txt artifacts/deps.zip`, then inspect the archive with `python3 -m zipfile -l artifacts/deps.zip`.

The script uses the `quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_28_x86_64` Docker image. Upload `artifacts/deps.zip` as **Python Libraries**. Do not claim that `deps.zip` exists unless the Docker build completed successfully.

## Upload Mapping

| Local artifact | Console field | Runtime behavior |
|---|---|---|
| `src/{{SINGLE_JOB_FILE}}` or `artifacts/{{JOB_ARCHIVE}}` | Python File Path (Python 文件地址) | Main Python job file or modular code ZIP |
| `artifacts/deps.zip` | Python Libraries | Added to the Python worker `PYTHONPATH` |
| {{PYTHON_ARCHIVES}} | Python Archives | Extracted in the Python worker working directory |
| {{ADDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY_FILES}} | Additional Dependency Files (附加依赖文件) | Available under `/flink/usrlib` |

Upload the applicable resources in **File Management** before creating the deployment.

## Deployment Parameters

| Console field | Value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Deployment mode (部署模式) | 流模式 | Stream mode is recommended |
| Deployment name (部署名称) | {{DEPLOYMENT_NAME}} | Confirmed job name |
| Engine version (引擎版本) | {{ENGINE_VERSION}} | Confirmed VVR version |
| Python File Path (Python 文件地址) | {{PYTHON_FILE_PATH}} | Uploaded `.py` or code `.zip` |
| Entry Module | {{ENTRY_MODULE_OR_EMPTY}} | Required for `.zip`; empty for `.py` |
| Entry Point Main Arguments | {{ENTRY_ARGUMENTS}} | Use `${secret_values.<VARIABLE_NAME>}` references here; keep credential values outside project files |
| Python Libraries | {{PYTHON_LIBRARIES}} | Third-party wheels or `deps.zip` |
| Python Archives | {{PYTHON_ARCHIVES}} | Custom environment or data archives |
| Additional Dependency Files (附加依赖文件) | {{ADDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY_FILES}} | Job files, data files, configuration, or connector JARs |

If this job uses a credential, first add it with the approved variable name under **Security > Variables (安全服务 > 变量管理)**. Then configure `--<argument-name> ${secret_values.<VARIABLE_NAME>}` in **Entry Point Main Arguments**. This expression is valid only in that console field. The Python job parses the selected argument name as a normal entry-point argument; project files record only the argument and variable names.

For Python 3.10 or 3.11 on supported VVR releases, document the confirmed runtime settings:

```yaml
python.executable: python3.10 (or python3.11)
python.client.executable: python3.10 (or python3.11)
```

If connector JARs are attached, document the confirmed `pipeline.classpaths` value here: `{{PIPELINE_CLASSPATHS}}`.

If the user uses or mentions LLM functions (llm.predict or llm.ai_* on DataFrame), guide the user to consider Flink AI Service (Flink AI 服务) for zero-configuration calls to managed models, and include the official documentation link: https://help.aliyun.com/zh/flink/realtime-flink/flink-ai-service.

## Deploy and Start

1. Upload every mapped artifact in File Management.
2. Open **Operations Center > Job Operations > Deploy Job > Python Job**.
3. Fill every parameter above and deploy the job.
4. Review deployment details and target-only checks.
5. Start the deployment separately when it is approved to go online.

